SmartKey — Dual License

This project uses a dual licensing model:

1. smartkey-core (crates/smartkey-core/)
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   See LICENSE-APACHE for the full text.

   This covers the core prediction engine: n-gram trie, Markov chain,
   CVM streaming counter, prefix matcher, and ensemble scorer. You may
   use smartkey-core in your own projects (mobile keyboards, IDE plugins,
   WASM apps, etc.) under the permissive Apache 2.0 terms.

2. Everything else (ibus/, corpus/, crates/smartkey-py/, tests/, config/)
   Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0.
   See LICENSE-GPL for the full text.

   This covers the IBus integration engine, corpus building tools,
   PyO3 bridge, and all application-level code. Derivative works that
   include these components must also be distributed under GPL 3.0.

Why dual license?
- Apache 2.0 for the library maximizes re-use and embedding (patent grant
  included — important for downstream consumers).
- GPL 3.0 for the application aligns with the IBus ecosystem and ensures
  that the full SmartKey input method remains open source.

